ie the movie is a  challenge sort of like the book is a  challenge to your icons your morality  how you perceive pop culture how you  perceive mythology and for that matter  how you perceive God everything in  Watchmen is filtered through pop culture  even history itself  when dr. Manhattan fights in the Vietnam  War Snyder recreates this historical  moment through the prism of the most  famous Vietnam War movie ever made  Apocalypse Now using the same music you  from Coppola film later Schneider uses  his soundtrack choices to reference the  art film Koyaanisqatsi life out of  balance  [Music]  that non-narrative film juxtaposes  beautiful scenes of nature with the  chaos of modern life an apt choice for a  man who left earth because of the mayhem  of humanity even the war room Richard  Nixon and his generals use is modeled  after a famous film fight it here this  is the war room all these examples  expose how we perceive and filter the  world through media and pop culture it's  not just a meta wink that Hollis Mason  has a copy of Moore's Watchmen on his  shelf it's yet another example of how  pop culture a comic book like Watchmen  influenced and shaped Snyder's and by  proxy our perception of the world  this theme culminates with Ozymandias  watching dozens of TV screens a la the  comic book but unlike Moore's original  intent  Ozymandias watching these screens  mirroring how viewers read the comic  Schneider instead uses this moment to  play on how reality is warped by pop  culture all the images on the screen  reference different films and programs  that influenced and shaped Zack Snyder  the filmmaker there's road warrior  Looney Tunes The Day the Earth Stood  Still  fail-safe and more so what are we to  make of Snyder's watchmen as the  filmmaker betrayed everything Alan  Moore's comics stood for glorifying it's  heroes and compromising the moral  ambiguity of Moore's work or has Snyder  skillfully adapted Watchmen for our pop  culture saturated time ultimately it all  depends on your perception if you view  Watchmen through the lens of Moore's  original intent then watchman's pretty  dumb but if you view the film through  Snyder's signature style and vision then  the film could be considered deep even  after all this we're still pretty split  on the merits of this movie but for what  it's worth I tend to lean towards the  deep side whereas many of our writers  lean towards dumb but honestly I can see  both sides so what do you think is  Watchmen deep or dumb as your perception  of the film changed it all let us know  in the comments below thanks to all our  patrons for supporting the channel and  our podcasts don't forget to subscribe  and we'll catch you next time guys and  before you go don't forget to check out  mischiefs new app go to ms CHF comm  click the link in the description or  just search ms CHF in the App Store or  on Google Play and as always thanks for  watching guys peace  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

